<% content_for :title do %>Privacy Policy – <%= EuroskyConfig::SITE_NAME %><% end %>

<%# Legal text is maintained in English only %>
<div class="eh-container">
  <article class="eh-narrow eh-doc eh-plain" lang="en">
    <p class="eh-sm"><a href="<%= root_path %>">&larr; Back to migration tool</a></p>

    <header class="eh-stack-xs">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="eh-sm eh-muted">Operated by: <strong><%= EuroskyConfig::OPERATOR_NAME %></strong> &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; Effective: <%= EuroskyConfig::EFFECTIVE_DATE %></p>
    </header>

    <div class="eh-well">
      <strong>Summary:</strong> This tool processes your ATProto credentials only for the duration of the migration.
      No data is sold, shared with third parties, or retained beyond the migration window.
    </div>

    <h2>1. Who We Are</h2>
    <p>
      This account migration service ("<strong>Service</strong>") is self-hosted software provided by
      <strong><%= EuroskyConfig::OPERATOR_NAME %></strong> ("<strong>Operator</strong>", "we", "us").
      Contact: <a href="mailto:<%= EuroskyConfig::OPERATOR_EMAIL %>"><%= EuroskyConfig::OPERATOR_EMAIL %></a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      The underlying migration tool is open-source software
      (<a href="<%= EuroskyConfig::REPO_URL %>" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><%= EuroskyConfig::REPO_URL %></a>).
      The Operator is the data controller for data processed through this hosted instance.
    </p>

    <h2>2. What Data We Collect</h2>
    <p>To perform a migration we temporarily collect and process:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Email address</strong> – used to send migration notifications and the PLC verification token.</li>
      <li><strong>Source account handle</strong> – your current Bluesky/ATProto handle (e.g. <code>alice.bsky.social</code>).</li>
      <li><strong>Source account access &amp; refresh tokens</strong> – obtained at login and stored encrypted (AES-256-GCM). Used to authenticate with your current PDS during the migration and deleted immediately upon completion.</li>
      <li><strong>Destination account access &amp; refresh tokens</strong> – obtained when your new account is created on the target PDS, stored encrypted (AES-256-GCM), and deleted immediately after a successful migration.</li>
      <li><strong>Target PDS host &amp; new handle</strong> – the destination Personal Data Server you are migrating to.</li>
      <li><strong>Invite code</strong> (if required by target PDS) – stored encrypted and deleted after account creation.</li>
      <li><strong>PLC token</strong> – the one-time verification token emailed to you; stored encrypted and expires within 1 hour.</li>
      <li><strong>Migration token</strong> – an unguessable identifier (e.g. <code>EURO-ABC12345</code>) generated to let you track migration progress. No personal data is embedded in this token.</li>
      <li><strong>Technical log data</strong> – server logs may contain IP addresses and timestamps for operational purposes.</li>
      <li><strong>Consent record</strong> – when you accept the Terms of Service and Privacy Policy, we store: your DID (a public identifier), a timestamp of your acceptance, a reference to the document versions you accepted, and your IP address (encrypted with AES-256-GCM). This is required by GDPR Art.&nbsp;7(1) to demonstrate that consent was given.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do <strong>not</strong> collect: browsing history, analytics beyond those disclosed below, or any data unrelated to the migration.</p>

    <h2>3. How We Use Your Data</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Execute the ATProto account migration on your behalf (the sole purpose).</li>
      <li>Send transactional emails (migration start, completion, PLC token, backup ready).</li>
      <li>Diagnose and recover from migration errors.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do <strong>not</strong> use your data for marketing, profiling, or any purpose beyond operating the migration.</p>

    <h2>4. Data Retention &amp; Deletion</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Access &amp; refresh tokens</strong>: Deleted immediately after a successful migration. Automatic cleanup jobs purge any remaining tokens every 6 hours.</li>
      <li><strong>PLC tokens</strong>: Deleted immediately after use or within 1 hour. Automatic cleanup jobs run every 6 hours.</li>
      <li><strong>Migration record</strong>: The non-sensitive migration record (status, timestamps, handle) may be retained for operational troubleshooting. Contact us to request deletion.</li>
      <li><strong>Email address</strong>: Retained only for the duration of the migration. Contact us to request deletion.</li>
      <li><strong>Backup bundles</strong> (if requested): Available for download for 24 hours, then automatically deleted from our server.</li>
      <li><strong>Server logs</strong>: Retained for up to <%= EuroskyConfig::LOG_RETENTION_DAYS %> days for operational security, then purged.</li>
      <li><strong>Consent records</strong>: Retained for up to 6 years as required by applicable EU statutes of limitations. These records contain only your DID (public), acceptance timestamp, document version references, and your encrypted IP address.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>5. Data Sharing</h2>
    <p>
      We do not sell, rent, or share your personal data with third parties, except:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Target PDS</strong>: Your account credentials are passed to the destination Personal Data Server you specify, which operates under its own privacy policy.</li>
      <li><strong>Source PDS (Bluesky / bsky.social)</strong>: The migration tool reads your repository data from your current PDS.</li>
      <li><strong>Email provider</strong>: Transactional emails are sent via the SMTP provider configured by the Operator.</li>
      <% if EuroskyConfig::HOSTING_PROVIDER_NAME.present? %>
      <li><strong>Infrastructure provider (<%= EuroskyConfig::HOSTING_PROVIDER_NAME %>)</strong>: Our hosting provider processes data on our behalf as a data processor under a GDPR Art.&nbsp;28 Data Processing Agreement. See Section&nbsp;6 for full details.</li>
      <% end %>
      <li><strong>Legal requirements</strong>: We may disclose data if required by applicable law.</li>
    </ul>

    <% if EuroskyConfig::HOSTING_PROVIDER_NAME.present? %>
    <h2>6. Hosting Infrastructure &amp; Sub-processors</h2>
    <p>
      This Service is hosted on infrastructure provided by
      <strong><%= EuroskyConfig::HOSTING_PROVIDER_NAME %></strong><% if EuroskyConfig::HOSTING_PROVIDER_ADDRESS.present? %>
      (<%= EuroskyConfig::HOSTING_PROVIDER_ADDRESS %>)<% end %>.
      This provider acts as a data processor under a Data Processing Agreement (DPA) concluded
      pursuant to Art.&nbsp;28 GDPR.
    </p>
    <p>
      Under this DPA, the hosting provider processes the following categories of personal data on
      our behalf: personal master data, communication data (e.g. email addresses), and technical
      log data, affecting end users of this service.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Data location:</strong> Data is processed within
      <strong><%= EuroskyConfig::HOSTING_PROVIDER_DATA_LOCATION %></strong>.
    </p>
    <% if EuroskyConfig::HOSTING_PROVIDER_SUBPROCESSORS_URL.present? %>
    <p>
      The hosting provider's approved sub-processors and data processing details are listed at:
      <a href="<%= EuroskyConfig::HOSTING_PROVIDER_SUBPROCESSORS_URL %>" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><%= EuroskyConfig::HOSTING_PROVIDER_SUBPROCESSORS_URL %></a>.
    </p>
    <% end %>
    <% end %>

    <h2>7. Security</h2>
    <p>
      Sensitive credentials are encrypted at rest using AES-256-GCM (Lockbox).
      Connections to this service use TLS. Rate limiting is applied to all endpoints.
      Despite these measures, no system is perfectly secure — use a strong, unique password.
    </p>
    <% if EuroskyConfig::HOSTING_PROVIDER_NAME.present? %>
    <p>
      Our hosting provider (<%= EuroskyConfig::HOSTING_PROVIDER_NAME %>) implements Technical and
      Organizational Measures (TOMs) in accordance with Art.&nbsp;32 GDPR.<% if EuroskyConfig::HOSTING_PROVIDER_CERTIFICATIONS.present? %>
      Certifications held: <strong><%= EuroskyConfig::HOSTING_PROVIDER_CERTIFICATIONS %></strong>.<% end %>
      <% if EuroskyConfig::HOSTING_PROVIDER_TOM_URL.present? %>
      Full TOM documentation:
      <a href="<%= EuroskyConfig::HOSTING_PROVIDER_TOM_URL %>" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><%= EuroskyConfig::HOSTING_PROVIDER_TOM_URL %></a>.
      <% end %>
    </p>
    <% end %>

    <h2>8. Your Rights</h2>
    <p>
      Depending on your jurisdiction (e.g. GDPR, CCPA) you may have the right to access, correct, or delete
      your personal data, or to object to certain processing. To exercise these rights, contact us at
      <a href="mailto:<%= EuroskyConfig::OPERATOR_EMAIL %>"><%= EuroskyConfig::OPERATOR_EMAIL %></a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Because credentials are deleted automatically within 48 hours, there is typically very little
      data to retrieve. We will respond within 30 days.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Cookies &amp; Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      This Service does not use tracking cookies. A session cookie is set by the Rails framework for
      CSRF protection only. No cross-site tracking occurs.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Children</h2>
    <p>This Service is not directed at children under 13 (or 16 in the EU). We do not knowingly collect data from minors.</p>

    <h2>11. Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy. Material changes will be announced on the migration page or via email
      (if you provided one). Continued use after changes constitutes acceptance.
    </p>

    <h2>12. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      <strong><%= EuroskyConfig::OPERATOR_NAME %></strong><br>
      Email: <a href="mailto:<%= EuroskyConfig::OPERATOR_EMAIL %>"><%= EuroskyConfig::OPERATOR_EMAIL %></a><br>
      <% if EuroskyConfig::OPERATOR_ADDRESS.present? %>
        Address: <%= EuroskyConfig::OPERATOR_ADDRESS %>
      <% end %>
    </p>
  </article>
</div>
